row: B12
flip: №952 — DONE
status: LEAK-SUITE NEGATIVE — `mlog check` REFUSES with [PII_EGRESS_OUTPUT]
  (the static line, the B1 machinery); the №952 RUNTIME twin refuses the
  SAME program with [SINK_CLEARANCE_RUNTIME] on BOTH backends when the
  static gate is silenced (METALOGOS_STATIC_LABEL_GATE_OFF=1).
why: the runtime value-label line (ADR-0156 §5) — the label rides the
  VALUE: the source marks it, the walk/join propagates it through pattern
  returns (the live summary walk), bindings, collections, entities and
  the kv sidecar, and the sink dispatcher checks it with the clearance
  rule the static gate applies.
note: the double line is the contract — static catches what it can SEE,
  the runtime catches what executes; neither can be silenced without the
  other still refusing the audited shapes.
history: on the PUBLISHED v0.39.0 the runtime had no value-label line at
  all — where the static lattice was blind, the leak executed (the audit
  of 12.11; the PoCs live in FOSVED-office-v2 →
  docs/projects/metalogos/audit_2026-11-12/).
